The probe function returns, but the process hangs during async executor shutdown after `asyncio.to_thread`. That explains the pytest hang. I’m going to avoid `asyncio.to_thread` here and use a short-lived daemon thread plus `asyncio.wait_for` around a future, so collect_preview remains bounded.
